# .env.example — copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   python3 env_config.py        # prints what was picked up, without secrets
#
# Precedence, highest first: an explicit CLI flag, then an exported
# environment variable, then this file, then the code's own default. A .env
# never overrides something you typed or something CI exported.
#
# Every value below is a PLACEHOLDER. env_config.py treats any value that
# still contains a `{...}` brace group as unset, so a copied example is never
# sent to an API as if it were a key — a 401 a long way from its cause is
# exactly what that rule exists to prevent.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWOCAPTCHA_KEY — one key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving,
# the Scraping Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY={your_2captcha_api_key}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLEEPNUMBER_PROXY — an exit address for the scraper's browser.
#
# THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL ON THIS SITE FROM OUTSIDE THE US. See the README's
# "Access" section: www.sleepnumber.com answers HTTP 403 from CloudFront to
# every request from the addresses measured so far, and the refusal is a
# property of the ADDRESS, not of the request — a bare curl, a full browser
# header set, a Googlebot user agent and a HEAD all get the identical 919-byte
# CloudFront "Request blocked" page.
#
# Pick a US exit: this is a US retailer and the block tracks geography.
#   http://{login}-zone-resi-region-us:{password}@proxy.2captcha.com:2334
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLEEPNUMBER_PROXY=http://{login}-zone-resi-region-us:{password}@proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLEEPNUMBER_CDP_ENDPOINT — the 2Captcha Scraping Browser API, over CDP.
#
# The remote browser brings its own exit, user agent and fingerprint, so the
# engines refuse --proxy and --fingerprint alongside this on purpose; stacking
# a second identity creates a contradiction rather than better cover.
#
# `country-` picks the exit country, `pid-` a profile with persistent cookies
# (ONE live connection each — use several pids rather than raising
# --concurrency). Profile credentials expire in about a day, so this is a
# SHAPE, not a working endpoint; mint a fresh one when you need it.
#   ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLEEPNUMBER_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLEEPNUMBER_URL — a default listing URL, used when --url is not given.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLEEPNUMBER_URL={a_sleepnumber_listing_url}
